# SYNTHETIC / DERIVED fixture. Two run graphs in ONE file, which is the shape
# that decides where the self-contradiction refusal may live.
#
# Construction, mechanical and in this order:
#   1. prober/state/task-4-e2e/run-2.nq verbatim (run 2026-08-27T10:00:00Z),
#      which declares data.kkg.kadaster.nl/query DORMANT and measures the
#      other two endpoints.
#   2. prober/state/task-4-e2e/run-1.nq with every occurrence of
#      2026-08-27T09:00:00Z rewritten to 2026-08-27T11:00:00Z, so it is the
#      LATER of the two runs. It measures all three endpoints, kadaster
#      included, and its dormancy section is empty (sw:dormantCount "0").
#
# So sweep 10:00 skipped kadaster and sweep 11:00 probed it. Under a weekly
# cadence for a dormant endpoint that pair is the NORMAL one, and it is how
# dormancy clears itself: the probe week measures the endpoint, its
# sw:currentRun advances to that run, that run carries no dormancy fact, and
# the marker is gone with no delete and no condition.
#
# This is therefore the fixture that proves the self-contradiction refusal must
# be per GRAPH and not per file. A per-file check would see "kadaster declared
# dormant" and "kadaster measured" in the same bytes and refuse a legitimate
# concatenation, which is what a run directory replayed with
# 'load_run.py STORE run-*.nq' hands the loader every time.
#
# 277 quads, two run graphs. Loading it must succeed, and kadaster's
# sw:currentRun must afterwards name the 11:00 run.
